    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d470">

                <pb facs="0486" n="1220" xml:id="pg1220"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr. Dupuy de Lôme.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-01-07"><hi rendition="#italic">January 7,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 65.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 31st ultimo, and beg to thank you for your courtesy in
                    telegraphing to the Captain-General of Cuba, urging him to endeavor, as far as
                    possible, to protect the property of Messrs. E. Atkins &amp; Co., of Boston,
                    from devastation.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
